        "role": "user",
        "content": "{\"context\":[{\"id\":\"c1\",\"text\":\"CAPITAL RESOURCES\"},{\"id\":\"c2\",\"text\":\"On July 17, 2025, we filed a shelf registration statement (the \\\"Shelf\\\") with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (the \\\"SEC\\\") which permits us to issue an unlimited amount of debt securities from time to time.\"},{\"id\":\"c3\",\"text\":\"The Shelf expires on July 17, 2028.\"},{\"id\":\"c4\",\"text\":\"On March 6, 2026, we entered into a 364-day committed credit facility agreement with a syndicate of banks, which provides for up to $1 billion of borrowings, with an option to increase borrowings up to $1.5 billion in total with lender approval.\"}],\"filing\":\"NKE 10-K\",\"section\":\"Part II Item 7\",\"sentences\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"The facility matures on March 5, 2027, with an option to extend the maturity date an additional 364 days.\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"This facility replaced the prior $1 billion 364-day credit facility agreement entered into on March 7, 2025, which matured on March 6, 2026.\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"On March 7, 2025, we entered into a five-year committed credit facility agreement with a syndicate of banks which provides for up to $2 billion of borrowings, with the option to increase borrowings up to $3 billion in total with lender approval.\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"The facility matures on March 7, 2030, with options to extend the maturity date up to an additional two years.\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"We currently have long-term debt ratings of A+ and A2 from S&P Global Ratings and Moody's Ratings, respectively.\"},{\"id\":\"s6\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"As it relates to our committed credit facilities entered into on March 6, 2026 and March 7, 2025, if our long-term debt ratings were to decline, the facility fees and interest rates may increase.\"},{\"id\":\"s7\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"Conversely, if our long-term debt ratings were to improve, the facility fees and interest rates may decrease.\"},{\"id\":\"s8\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"Changes in our long-term debt ratings would not trigger acceleration of maturity of any then-outstanding borrowings or any future borrowings under the committed credit facilities.\"},{\"id\":\"s9\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"Under these facilities, we have agreed to various covenants.\"},{\"id\":\"s10\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"These covenants include limits on the disposal of assets and the amount of debt secured by liens we may incur.\"},{\"id\":\"s11\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"In the event we were to have any borrowings outstanding under these facilities, failed to meet any covenant and were unable to obtain a waiver from a majority of the banks in the applicable syndicate, any borrowings would become immediately due and payable.\"},{\"id\":\"s12\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"As of May 31, 2026, we were in full compliance with each of these covenants, and we believe it is unlikely we will fail to meet any of these covenants in the foreseeable future.\"},{\"id\":\"s13\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"Liquidity is also provided by our $3 billion commercial paper program.\"},{\"id\":\"s14\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"As of and for the fiscal years ended May 31, 2026 and 2025, we did not have any borrowings outstanding under our $3 billion program.\"},{\"id\":\"s15\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > CAPITAL RESOURCES\",\"text\":\"We may issue commercial paper or other debt securities depending on general corporate needs.\"}]}"
      }
